course: dictionary
lesson: 13807
title: Iowa, a farming state in the USA
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Iowa is a name, so it always starts with a capital letter. It is the name of a place: a state in the middle of the United States of America. A state is a large part of a country, a bit like a county in the UK. «Maya's uncle grows maize on his farm in Iowa.» The word Iowa tells you where the farm is.
explain: Look for clues around the name. «Iowa farmers keep thousands of pigs and grow fields of maize.» The words farmers, pigs and maize tell you what Iowa is known for: farming. When you see a name like this, ask: is it a person, a place, or a thing? Here it is a place.
explain: Use a map to check. The Midwest is the middle part of the USA. Iowa is found there, so it is not on the coast. «The state of Iowa has its capital in Des Moines.» Capital means the city where the state government meets.
fact: Iowa is a state in the middle of the United States of America.
fact: Iowa is in the Midwest, the middle part of the USA.
fact: Iowa is known for farms, maize (corn) and pigs.
fact: The capital city of Iowa is Des Moines.
fact: Iowa is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital letter.
exercise: «Maya's uncle is a farmer in Iowa, where he grows maize.» What is Iowa? | A country in Europe | *A state in the middle of the United States | A kind of farm animal | A city in Scotland
exercise: «Iowa» is written with a capital I. Why? | Because it is a very long word | Because it is a farm animal | Because it is the first word of every sentence | *Because it is the name of a place
exercise: «Iowa farmers grow a lot of maize.» What is maize also called? | Potatoes | Wheat | *Corn | Rice
test: Ella reads, «Many farms in Iowa keep pigs.» What does Iowa mean in this sentence? | A farmer | A food | A pig | *A place
test: «The capital of Iowa is Des Moines.» Which city is the capital of Iowa? | Chicago | New York | Los Angeles | *Des Moines
exam: Dad says, «We will fly to Iowa for the summer, then drive out to see the farms.» Where are they going? | Scotland | *The middle of the United States | Australia | Canada
